# A virtualenv is also unpaired when it is a symlink into another checkout (a git worktree points at control's).
# The trailing-slash patterns above match a directory only, so without the bare names a `git add -A` in a worktree
# can track `.venv` as a symlink and overwrite a real `.venv` directory on merge.

